{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kd_character_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kd_character_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L127-L141","doc":"Equality holds only at the classical point `q = 1`, so the obstruction is\nstrict everywhere the substrate actually sits (`q₀ ≈ 1.10998`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kd_holonomy_cannot_realise_subunit_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kd_holonomy_cannot_realise_subunit_correction","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**The punchline.** With `ħ = 2 ln q` at real `q > 0`, the holonomy character\nis `(q + q⁻¹)/2 ≥ 1`, so it cannot equal a correction strictly below 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.kd_character_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.kd_character_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L109-L115","doc":"The Kohno–Drinfeld character at the substrate's real `q`, elementarily:\n`(q + q⁻¹)/2 − 1 = (q−1)²/(2q)`. A square over a positive, so the character never\ndrops below 1 — no analysis, no transcendence, no appeal to `cosh`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.correction_below_one_excludes_real_spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.correction_below_one_excludes_real_spectrum","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**Hence a sub-unit correction excludes every real-spectrum holonomy.** The\nmeasured correction is `0.998…< 1`, so no real `a` reproduces it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.real_spectrum_character_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.real_spectrum_character_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**A holonomy with real spectrum has character at least 1.** If the generator's\neigenvalues are `±a` with `a` real, the normalised character `tr M / 2` is\n`cosh a ≥ 1`.\n\nThis is the residue-independent step: it is quantified over **all** real `a`, so a\n`q`-dependent residue only changes which `a` occurs and the bound is unmoved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.two_le_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.two_le_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HolonomySpectrumSignObstruction.lean#L79-L86","doc":"`x + x⁻¹ ≥ 2` for positive `x` — the whole obstruction in one line, and the\nreason it cannot be evaded by choosing residues: it holds for *every* positive\n`x`, so every real generator eigenvalue is caught. ","signatureChunk":0}]}